quran[7]{c,v,t}:
  11,82,"So when Our command came, We turned their town upside down and rained down upon them stones of baked clay, layer upon layer,"
  11,83,marked by your Lord. And this (town) is not far from the wrongdoers (of Mecca).
  11,84,"And to Madyan (Midian), (We sent) their (fellow) brother Shu‘ayb. He said: ‘O my people! Worship Allah. You have no god other than Him. And do not give short measure nor less weight. Indeed, I see you prospering, but I fear the punishment of an encompassing day for you."
  11,85,"O my people! Give full measure and weigh justly. And do not curtail people’s goods. And do not act wickedly on the earth, causing corruption."
  11,86,"Whatever lasts with Allah is better for you if you are believers, and I am not a keeper over you.’"
  11,87,"They said: ‘O Shu‘ayb! Does your prayer tell you that we should abandon what our forefathers have been worshipping or not manage our properties as we wish? Indeed, you are a gentle and sensible person.’"
  11,88,"He said: ‘O my people! Just tell me: If I stand upon a clear proof from my Lord, and He has provided me with sound means of livelihood from Himself (then why should I hesitate to convey the truth to you)? I do not want to follow you (by doing the same thing), which I forbid you to do. I only desire to reform (the matters) as far as I can. And my success lies only with Allah. In Him, I put my trust, and to Him, I turn penitently."
